      "author": {
        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-20T17:40:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is generally encouraged to use providers here instead of returning a pointer to the `dep` directly. https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CrogPUm7x6yOO149Cp35tlqAB3ZdeGzApLpWBh6PXO0/edit#heading\u003dh.m6ed3b1qks0h\n\nInstead of returning `[]android.Module` from this function, is it possible to just return `[]cc.SharedLibraryInfo`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 484,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 484,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "431ddf9b7647a88bf36b004d94bfaff940c1f92b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c75f08a_266d4a18",
        "filename": "cc/fuzz.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 484,
      "author": {
        "id": 1868610
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-20T19:02:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looked into it based on your comment. If there is no `SharedLibrary` field in the `sharedLibInfo` object, we would like to mention the dependency name and type for the Java fuzzer dependency, to make it easy to debug. However, these fields are not present in the `sharedLibInfo` object, but are present in the `dep` object. So, can we please return the `dep` pointer directly, or do you strongly recommend not to do so?",
      "parentUuid": "9d2d6179_8510070a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 484,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 484,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "431ddf9b7647a88bf36b004d94bfaff940c1f92b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "714e0246_c59ddcab",
        "filename": "cc/fuzz.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 484,
      "author": {
